.3,"liab_to_assets":5.4,"cash_to_assets":69.8,"current_ratio":19.85,"roe":31.5,"roa":29.9,"moat":{"ticker":"PTGX","period":"2026Q3","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"生技產業的產品定價權高度依賴臨床試驗結果與藥證核准，Protagonist Therapeutics 在此階段尚未有成熟的商業化產品，因此品牌與定價能力尚未顯現。其價值主要體現在研發管線的潛力，而非現有的市場定價能力。與消費品牌或成熟工業品相比，其品牌價值與定價權壁壘極為薄弱，易受科學突破或競爭者產品影響。","comment_en":"In the biotech industry, pricing power is highly dependent on clinical trial outcomes and regulatory approvals. Protagonist Therapeutics has not yet commercialized mature products, thus brand and pricing power are not yet evident. Its value lies primarily in the potential of its R&D pipeline, not existing market pricing capabilities. Compared to consumer brands or established industrial goods, its brand value and pricing power barriers are extremely weak, easily influenced by scientific breakthroughs or competitor products."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":9,"comment_zh":"Protagonist Therapeutics 的核心價值建立在專利保護的研發成果上。其針對特定疾病機轉的創新療法，若能取得藥證，將享有獨特的市場地位。專利是生技產業最重要的壁壘，能提供一段時間的市場獨占期，免受仿製藥競爭。然而，專利的有效性與持續性仍需關注其專利布局的廣度與深度，以及未來是否面臨挑戰。","comment_en":"Protagonist Therapeutics' core value is built upon R&D achievements protected by patents. Its innovative therapies targeting specific disease mechanisms, if approved, will enjoy a unique market position. Patents are the most crucial barrier in the biotech industry, providing a period of market exclusivity against generic competition. However, patent validity and longevity require attention to the breadth and depth of its patent portfolio and potential future challenges."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"生技藥物的轉換成本主要體現在患者對療效的依賴以及醫療體系對新藥的採用流程。一旦 Protagonist Therapeutics 的藥物被證實有效且安全，患者和醫生轉換到其他療法的意願會降低。然而，此類轉換成本並非絕對，仍受新一代藥物出現、健保給付條件變動等因素影響，壁壘相對較弱。","comment_en":"Switching costs for biotech drugs are mainly reflected in patient reliance on efficacy and the healthcare system's adoption process for new drugs. Once Protagonist Therapeutics' drugs are proven effective and safe, patients and doctors will be less willing to switch to other therapies. However, these switching costs are not absolute and are still influenced by factors such as the emergence of next-generation drugs and changes in insurance coverage, making the barrier relatively weak."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Protagonist Therapeutics 作為一家生技製藥公司，其商業模式不涉及直接的網絡效應。產品的成功主要取決於科學的有效性、臨床數據和市場接受度，而非用戶間的互動或網絡擴張。因此，在網絡效應這一維度上，公司幾乎沒有任何護城河可言。","comment_en":"As a biopharmaceutical company, Protagonist Therapeutics' business model does not involve direct network effects. Product success depends primarily on scientific efficacy, clinical data, and market acceptance, rather than user interactions or network expansion. Therefore, in terms of network effects, the company possesses virtually no moat."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"生技產業的規模經濟主要體現在研發投入的攤薄和生產效率的提升。Protagonist Therapeutics 若能成功商業化其管線，隨著銷售額的增長，其單位生產成本有望下降。然而，相較於成熟產業，生技產業的規模優勢相對有限，且研發的高不確定性使得成本優勢難以成為穩固的護城河。","comment_en":"Economies of scale in the biotech industry are mainly reflected in the amortization of R&D investments and improvements in production efficiency. If Protagonist Therapeutics successfully commercializes its pipeline, its unit production costs are expected to decrease as sales grow. However, compared to mature industries, the scale advantage in biotech is relatively limited, and the high uncertainty of R&D makes cost advantages difficult to establish as a stable moat."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Protagonist Therapeutics 的業務模式並非建立在獨特的地理位置或特定資產之上。其價值核心是知識產權和研發能力，這些是無形的，不受地理限制。因此，在獨特地理資產這一維度上，公司不具備任何護城河。","comment_en":"Protagonist Therapeutics' business model is not built upon unique geographical locations or specific assets. Its core value lies in intellectual property and R&D capabilities, which are intangible and not geographically constrained. Therefore, the company possesses no moat in terms of unique geographical assets."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Protagonist Therapeutics 的高 ROE (31.5%) 和 ROA (29.9%)，以及強勁的 F-Score (8/9) 和健康的現金部位（現金 $800.1M / 負債 $8.6M），顯示其在研發和營運管理上具有相當高的效率。儘管尚未有成熟產品，但其資源配置和財務結構顯示出卓越的營運能力，為未來的商業化奠定良好基礎。","comment_en":"Protagonist Therapeutics' high ROE (31.5%) and ROA (29.9%), along with a strong F-Score (8/9) and healthy cash position (Cash $800.1M / Debt $8.6M), indicate considerable efficiency in R&D and operational management. Although it lacks mature products, its resource allocation and financial structure demonstrate excellent operational capability, laying a solid foundation for future commercialization."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"公司擁有充裕的現金儲備，且負債極低，顯示其在資本配置上具有極大的靈活性。高 ROE 和 ROA 反映了管理層能有效地將資本投入到高回報的研發項目中。其資本配置策略似乎專注於推進研發管線，這在生技產業是常見且必要的，若能持續成功，將是重要的護城河。","comment_en":"The company possesses ample cash reserves with extremely low debt, indicating significant flexibility in capital allocation. High ROE and ROA reflect management's ability to effectively invest capital into high-return R&D projects. Its capital allocation strategy appears focused on advancing the R&D pipeline, which is common and necessary in the biotech industry. If successful, this will be a significant moat."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"生技藥物的客戶留存主要取決於藥物的療效和安全性。一旦患者對 Protagonist Therapeutics 的藥物產生依賴，且無更好替代品，則客戶留存率會相對較高。然而，這並非傳統意義上的品牌忠誠度，而是基於臨床效果的結果，易受新技術或新藥的挑戰，因此壁壘不高。","comment_en":"Customer retention for biotech drugs primarily depends on the drug's efficacy and safety. Once patients become reliant on Protagonist Therapeutics' drugs and lack better alternatives, retention rates will be relatively high. However, this is not brand loyalty in the traditional sense but is based on clinical outcomes, making it susceptible to challenges from new technologies or drugs, thus the barrier is not high."},"m10_durability":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Protagonist Therapeutics 的護城河主要來自其專利保護的創新療法，這提供了相當程度的持久性。然而，生技產業的技術迭代速度快，專利終有到期日，且臨床試驗結果具有不確定性。若其研發管線能持續產出突破性產品，則其持久性將得到加強。目前來看，其專利壁壘提供了較為穩固的長期價值。","comment_en":"Protagonist Therapeutics' moat primarily stems from its patent-protected innovative therapies, which provide a considerable degree of durability. However, the biotech industry experiences rapid technological iteration, patents eventually expire, and clinical trial results are inherently uncertain. If its R&D pipeline can continuously produce breakthrough products, its durability will be strengthened. Currently, its patent barrier offers relatively stable long-term value."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Protagonist Therapeutics 的經濟護城河主要建立在專利保護的創新研發能力上，這使其在 M2（專利/特許）和 M8（資本配置）方面獲得較高評價。其高 ROE/ROA 和健康的財務狀況（M7、M8）顯示了卓越的營運效率和資本運用能力。然而，在品牌定價權（M1）、網絡效應（M4）、規模成本（M5）和地理資產（M6）等方面，公司幾乎沒有護城河。其價值高度依賴於研發的成功與藥證的取得，這使得其護城河的持久性（M10）雖有專利支撐，但仍面臨生技產業快速變化的風險。整體而言，其護城河屬於專利驅動的特許經營模式，但尚處於早期發展階段，未來成長潛力與風險並存。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Protagonist Therapeutics' economic moat is primarily built upon its patent-protected innovative R&D capabilities, earning it high marks in M2 (Patents/Regulatory) and M8 (Capital Allocation). Its high ROE/ROA and healthy financial status (M7, M8) demonstrate excellent operational efficiency and capital utilization. However, the company possesses virtually no moat in areas like brand pricing power (M1), network effects (M4), cost advantages of scale (M5), and geographical assets (M6). Its value is highly dependent on R&D success and drug approvals, making its moat's durability (M10), while supported by patents, still subject to the risks of rapid change in the biotech industry. Overall, its moat resembles a patent-driven franchise model, but it is still in an early development stage, with both growth potential and risks coexisting.","evidenceHash":"d2200cba6dfade9fdf1a1eb72900975d8c14a8e86a4c538489d625d5184a01c0","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null,"evidenceHash":"d2200cba6dfade9fdf1a1eb72900975d8c14a8e86a4c538489d625d5184a01c0","currentEvidenceHash":"d2200cba6dfade9fdf1a1eb72900975d8c14a8e86a4c538489d625d5184a01c0"},"fScore":{"score":8,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T12:41:57.622Z","evidenceHash":"2d83445159a114580eb7cf94a25dff16ec2c0b37de1504a755eede5a9049933a"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-08T12:41:57.622Z","evidenceHash":"2d83445159a114580eb7cf94a25dff16ec2c0b37de1504a755eede5a9049933a"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/PTGX.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/PTGX.png","website":"https://www.protagonist-inc.com","ceo":"Dinesh V. Patel","full_time_employees":"132","description":"Protagonist Therapeutics, Inc. is a biopharmaceutical firm dedicated to discovering and advancing peptide-based therapies. Their research primarily focuses on treatments for hematological and blood conditions, as well as inflammatory and immune-mediated disorders. The company's pipeline features rusfertide (PTG-300), an injectable hepcidin mimetic currently undergoing Phase II clinical trials for the management of polycythemia vera, hereditary hemochromatosis, and other blood-related ailments. Also in Phase II development is PN-943, an oral peptide engineered as a specific antagonist of alpha-4-beta-7 integrin, intended for addressing inflammatory bowel disease (IBD). Furthermore, they are progressing PN-235, an orally administered antagonist specifically targeting the interleukin-23 receptor, designed for both IBD and various non-IBD therapeutic applications. Protagonist Therapeutics maintains a licensing and collaborative agreement with Janssen Biotech, Inc. Founded in 2006, the company's headquarters are located in Newark, California.","description_en":"Protagonist Therapeutics, Inc. is a biopharmaceutical firm dedicated to discovering and advancing peptide-based therapies. Their research primarily focuses on treatments for hematological and blood conditions, as well as inflammatory and immune-mediated disorders. The company's pipeline features rusfertide (PTG-300), an injectable hepcidin mimetic currently undergoing Phase II clinical trials for the management of polycythemia vera, hereditary hemochromatosis, and other blood-related ailments. Also in Phase II development is PN-943, an oral peptide engineered as a specific antagonist of alpha-4-beta-7 integrin, intended for addressing inflammatory bowel disease (IBD). Furthermore, they are progressing PN-235, an orally administered antagonist specifically targeting the interleukin-23 receptor, designed for both IBD and various non-IBD therapeutic applications. Protagonist Therapeutics maintains a licensing and collaborative agreement with Janssen Biotech, Inc. Founded in 2006, the company's headquarters are located in Newark, California.","description_zh":"Protagonist Therapeutics, Inc.（美股代碼：PTGX）為 Healthcare 領域之重要企業，專注於 Biotechnology 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"7707 Gateway Boulevard","city":"Newark","state":"CA","zip":"94560","country":"US","phone":"510 474 0170","full_address":"7707 Gateway Boulevard, Newark, CA 94560, US","range_52w":"77-160.81","year_high":160.81,"year_low":77,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":77,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-02","name":"Ali Asif","title":"officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":5312,"price":12.17,"total_val":0.06},{"date":"2026-10-02","name":"Ali Asif","title":"officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":15650,"price":19.19,"total_val":0.3},{"date":"2026-10-02","name":"Ali Asif","title":"officer: Chief Financ